{"explanation":"Adds a repeated public-API encryption/decryption round-trip regression test. Each independently encrypted record must decrypt with its own retained GCM parameters and AAD-protected algorithm metadata; the test intentionally does not compare randomized ciphertext, nonce, or parameter bytes. Existing test methods, signatures, and assertions are preserved unchanged.","review_assumptions":["EncryptedKey does not expose its retained AlgorithmParameters through its public API, so successful independent decryptions are the available non-reflective evidence that each encrypted record retains parameters usable by decrypt.","Supported Android providers accept the coordinated explicit GCMParameterSpec setup and preserve a decryptable AlgorithmParameters representation.","Persisted encrypted-record format compatibility is preserved by the coordinated EncryptedKey implementation and is outside this test-only edit's authorized behavior change."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"high","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java","original_code":"    @Test
