","edit_kind":"test","corrected_code":"    @Test
    public void testUTF8() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        String plaintxt = "火尸木火1十寥日烤";
        SecretKey key = generateKey("AES");

        byte[] plaintxt_encoded = plaintxt.getBytes();

        SecretKey plaintxt_key = new SecretKeySpec(plaintxt_encoded, "AES");
        EncryptedKey ek = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, plaintxt_key);

        SecretKey sk = ek.decrypt(key);
        byte[] decryptedBytes = sk.getEncoded();
        String decryptedText = new String(decryptedBytes, StandardCharsets.UTF_8);

        assertEquals(plaintxt, decryptedText);
    }

    @Test
    public void testRepeatedEncryptionRoundTrips() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        SecretKey key = generateKey("AES");
        SecretKey firstPlaintext = generateKey("HmacSHA512");
        SecretKey secondPlaintext = generateKey("HmacSHA512");

        EncryptedKey firstEncrypted = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, firstPlaintext);
        EncryptedKey secondEncrypted = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, secondPlaintext);

        SecretKey firstDecrypted = firstEncrypted.decrypt(key);
        SecretKey secondDecrypted = secondEncrypted.decrypt(key);

        Assert.assertArrayEquals(firstPlaintext.getEncoded(), firstDecrypted.getEncoded());
        assertEquals(firstPlaintext.getAlgorithm(), firstDecrypted.getAlgorithm());
        Assert.assertArrayEquals(secondPlaintext.getEncoded(), secondDecrypted.getEncoded());
        assertEquals(secondPlaintext.getAlgorithm(), secondDecrypted.getAlgorithm());
    }
","reason":"Exercises two independent EncryptedKey encryption/decryption records through the unchanged public interface. Successful decryption of each record verifies that its retained GCM parameters remain available to decrypt and that AAD-protected key encodings and algorithms round-trip, without asserting randomized ciphertext, nonce, or parameter values.","symbol":"EncryptedKeyTest encryption/decryption test cases"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["EncryptedKeyTest preserves the existing key-encoding and algorithm assertions in test() and the existing UTF-8 round-trip assertion in testUTF8().","EncryptedKeyTest additionally verifies that two independently encrypted records decrypt to their respective original key encodings and algorithms through unchanged EncryptedKey.encrypt and EncryptedKey.decrypt entry points."],"required_contracts":["EncryptedKey.encrypt must retain its public name, parameter order, return type, and checked-exception behavior.","EncryptedKey.encrypt must use explicit fresh GCM parameters while retaining decryptable parameters and authenticating the protected-key algorithm as AAD.","Supported Android providers must support the coordinated explicit GCMParameterSpec encryption path and retained AlgorithmParameters decryption path."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java","required_tests":["Compile mobile androidTest sources to confirm the added test's GeneralSecurityException and IOException declarations cover the EncryptedKey API's checked exceptions.","Run EncryptedKeyTest on supported Android providers, including testRepeatedEncryptionRoundTrips, to verify independent AES/GCM records decrypt with retained parameters and restore both encoding and algorithm."]}
